OWED: `full` retains producer custody — send's param consumes <live!> ONLY on `ok`; on `full` the binding stays obligated and the arm's own dispose(s) discharges it. The verdict is the custody transfer point. TODAY: send never consumes at all (plain-copy semantics) — c stays obligated producer-side regardless of verdict, so dispose(c) in the full arm happens to work, but for the wrong reason; under transit semantics this pin is the regression wall against verdict-eating custody.
